@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: why a `kind: sandbox` Kit can declare NO credential and still reach a prompt, and the rung that catches it
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (agentCredentials, Spec, storedSecretNames)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/own_agent_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/provider_gate_test.go
' covers: e2e/ladder_test.go
' covers: internal/sbx/kit.go (KitCredential, KitCredAPIKey, KitCredInject)
' The mixin-era account this SUPERSEDES for the own-agent path:
'   _spec/internal/sbx/credential-path.puml — still correct for a mixin, and its
'   "sbx.Kit has no Credentials field, deliberately" no longer holds here.
' The capability record that reintroduced the block: _spec/_experiments/sbx-kit-capabilities.puml (E2)
' The domain grammar the allowlist speaks: _spec/internal/sbx/kit-domain-form.puml
' The ladder this adds a rung to: _spec/_paradigms/capability-ladder.puml
' Notes here are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── THE INCIDENT THIS FILE EXISTS FOR ──────────────────────────────────────
' Session proveo-1788935973-18915, target cecli, 2026-09-08T23:39. The session
' started, printed its posture, reached a prompt, and held. Then `/model xai`
' froze the TUI with a 403 on api.x.ai. Its own posture had said:
'
'     broker: 4 providers injected at the egress layer
'             (anthropic, openai, xai, google)
'     egress tier            allow-all
'     enforced by            sbx — Kit network allowlist + credential proxy
'
' Every one of those lines describes proveo's INTENT. None of them was measured
' against the Kit that was actually written.
'
' ── WHAT THE KIT ACTUALLY CARRIED (rendered, not inferred) ─────────────────
' `Spec` was run for that exact key set in both states of sbx's secret store:
'
'   sbx secret ls holds nothing under a service name  -> NO credentials: block
'   sbx secret ls holds anthropic openai xai google   -> four proxyManaged
'                                                        entries, inject rules
'                                                        per host
'
' The allowlist is identical either way: x.ai, *.x.ai, anthropic.com,
' *.anthropic.com, openai.com, *.openai.com, generativelanguage.googleapis.com.
' So REACH is granted for a provider whose credential is never declared, and
' that asymmetry is the whole defect.
'
' ── WHY THE STORE NEVER SATISFIES THE GATE BY ITSELF ───────────────────────
' `agentCredentials` declares a service only when `sbx secret ls` already holds
' one under the SERVICE name, and the vendor reference is explicit about why:
' "service — Credential identifier, matched against the value stored with
' `sbx secret set`. Lowercase kebab-case."
'
' proveo stores under the ENV VAR name — `sbx secret set --force XAI_API_KEY` —
' and refuses to store under the service name ON PURPOSE. That refusal is
' pinned: TestSpecNeverStoresAServiceNamedSecret, whose message records the
' measurement behind it ("overwriting whatever the operator has there —
' measured doing exactly that to an OAuth login").
'
' So the two names never meet, and nothing in a normal run makes them meet.
' `sbx secret set xai` is an OPERATOR action proveo does not and should not
' perform. The default state of any host proveo has not been hand-primed on is
' therefore: allowlist yes, credential no.
'
' ── AND THE VARIABLE IS NOT UNSET, WHICH IS WHAT HIDES IT ──────────────────
' credential-path.puml settled D1 against sbx v0.39.0: sbx does NOT export
' service secrets as environment variables. With no credentials: block, the
' agent should therefore hold XAI_API_KEY UNSET, and an unset key is a quiet
' no-op — cecli skips a provider it has no key for.
'
' It was not unset. The same run warned why, in its own output:
'
'     .env is inside the sandbox workspace and holds a provider key — the
'     agent's prelude sources it with `set -a`, so the key becomes agent
'     environment whatever egress tier you picked
'
' The workspace `.env` is a SECOND credential path, already recorded in
' credential-path.puml, and it is the one that fired. The brokered path
' delivered nothing; the mounted file delivered the real key; the two are
' invisible to each other.
'
' ── THE 403 IS NOT THE PROVIDER'S (measured) ───────────────────────────────
' api.x.ai was probed directly with three auth shapes:
'
'     no Authorization header   401  unauthenticated:no-credentials
'     "Bearer" with no value    401  unauthenticated:bad-credentials
'     "Bearer proveo-brokered"  400  Incorrect API key provided.
'
' 403 is not in xAI's auth vocabulary. So a 403 on api.x.ai is a PROXY verdict,
' and the sandbox proxy's own wording is the tell — upstream reports it as
' "Blocked by network policy: domain <host>:443 … no matching allow rule".
'
' NOT SETTLED HERE, and named rather than assumed:
'   WHICH RULE fired. The run captured it —
'     ~/.local/state/proveo/egress/<sid>/sbx/policy-log.json — and
'     `sbx policy log <sandbox>` answers live. Neither was read.
'   WHETHER A BARE HOST NEEDS :443. docker/sbx-releases#319 shows an agent's own
'     domain blocked until allowed as "opencode.ai:443,*.opencode.ai:443", and
'     #140/#189 report kit allow rules not taking effect at all. The kit
'     reference lists a bare host as ENFORCED, so this is testable, not decided.
'   WHETHER `*.x.ai` IS ACCEPTED IN inject[].domain. Still open from
'     kit-domain-form.puml; the probe that proved suffix domains PARSE never
'     asked whether they MATCH.
'
' ── WHAT cecli CONTRIBUTES, AND IT IS ONLY VISIBILITY ──────────────────────
' Measured against cecli 1.4.1 directly, with the completion path executed:
'   ONE call. `/model` completion walks the 63 slugs in
'     cecli/resources/providers.json and probes each whose api_key_env is set.
'     Of this run's keys only XAI_API_KEY appears there — anthropic, openai and
'     google are served by cecli's own static catalogue — so the completer makes
'     exactly one request: GET https://api.x.ai/v1/models, timeout 10s.
'   NEVER NEGATIVELY CACHED. `_update_cache` leaves the entry None on failure
'     and `_ensure_content` refetches whenever it is falsy, so it repeats on
'     every keystroke.
'   PRINTED OVER THE PROMPT. The failure is a bare `print()` from a
'     ThreadedCompleter worker while prompt_toolkit owns the screen.
'   NO OFFLINE FALLBACK. cecli's static catalogue holds ZERO xai/grok entries,
'     so `/model xai` offers 2 candidates when the probe answers 200 and 0 when
'     it answers 403. The menu can never populate.
' None of that is proveo's to fix, and none of it is the cause. A different
' agent on the same Kit fails differently and just as quietly.
'
' ── WHY THE LADDER SAID NOTHING ────────────────────────────────────────────
' Every rung asserts one property: the session reached a prompt and stayed
' alive for the hold window. This session did both. The ladder would have
' reported PASS for every rung, including the one that carries the Kit.
'
' The gap is not a missing rung. It is that no rung ever USES the agent. A
' credential that is never spent and a domain that is never fetched cannot fail
' a test that only watches for a prompt.
'
' THE FIX IS ONE PARAMETER. `holdSbxSession` takes a prompt string:
'   ""            today's behaviour, exactly — reach a prompt, hold, assert
'                 nothing about what the agent can do
'   any string    typed into the PTY once the prompt is reached, then the render
'                 is scanned for the refusals below for the rest of the hold
'
' PROVEO_LADDER_PROMPT carries it, so a climb stays a climb by default and
' becomes a first-use test when an operator names one. `/model xai` is the
' string that reproduces this incident; `PROVEO_LADDER_PROMPT` is deliberately
' free text, because the next incident will need a different one.
'
' ── THE MARKERS, AND WHY EACH EARNS ITS PLACE ──────────────────────────────
'   Blocked by network policy    the three wordings sandboxd's own docs give
'   Blocked by org policy        a block, one per rule origin: default policy,
'   Blocked by local rule for    org policy, and a developer-added local deny
'   no matching allow rule       the detail line a default-deny block carries
'   403 Client Error             what raise_for_status renders in any Python
'                                agent, and NOT a provider auth answer
'   Failed to fetch              cecli's model-list probe, the render measured
'   Incorrect API key provided   the sentinel reached the provider UNREPLACED,
'                                which is the injection failure, not a block
' A marker list is a liability if it grows by guess, so each line names the
' thing that produced it. `Incorrect API key provided` is the load-bearing one:
' it is the ONLY render that distinguishes "the proxy blocked me" from "the
' proxy let me through without injecting", and those have different owners.
title kind: sandbox credentials — reach without a credential,\nand the rung that spends one

package "internal/backend/sandbox" as PKG <<host>> {
  component "Spec\nbuilds allow from in.Detected" as SPEC <<app>>
  component "agentCredentials\ngated on stored[SERVICE]" as GATE <<app>>
}

database "sbx secret store\nHOST-WIDE" as STORE <<db>>

package "the Kit proveo writes" as KIT <<host>> {
  component "permissions.network.allow\n""x.ai"", ""*.x.ai""" as ALLOW <<app>>
  component "credentials[]\nEMPTY on any un-primed host" as CREDS <<error>>
}

component "workspace .env\nsourced with ""set -a""" as DOTENV <<error>>
component "the agent\n""XAI_API_KEY"" = the REAL key" as AGENT <<app>>
cloud "sbx proxy" as PROXY <<cloud>>
component "**403** on ""api.x.ai""\nread as the provider's refusal" as BUG <<error>>
component "e2e ladder\nPROVEO_LADDER_PROMPT" as LADDER <<app>>

SPEC ARROW_MAIN ALLOW : reach, unconditionally
SPEC ARROW_MAIN GATE
STORE ARROW_OPTIONAL GATE : holds ""XAI_API_KEY"",\nnever ""xai""
GATE ARROW_ERROR CREDS : declares nothing
DOTENV ARROW_ERROR AGENT : the path that actually delivers
AGENT ARROW_CLOUD PROXY : Bearer <real key>, no injection
PROXY ARROW_ERROR BUG
LADDER ARROW_MAIN AGENT : types the prompt, scans the render
BUG ARROW_QUEUE LADDER : the marker that fails the rung

note bottom of CREDS
  **The two names never meet.** sbx resolves
  ""service"" against ""sbx secret set xai"";
  proveo stores ""XAI_API_KEY"" and refuses the
  service name on purpose. So the default is
  allowlist yes, credential no.
end note

note top of ALLOW
  **Reach is granted before the gate runs.**
  ""allow"" comes from ""in.Detected"", the
  credential from ""stored[]"" — different inputs,
  one direction. A host can be reachable with
  nothing to authenticate it.
end note

note bottom of DOTENV
  **A second credential path, unaware of the
  first.** The brokered path delivered nothing
  and the mounted file delivered the real key.
  Neither can see the other, so the posture line
  and the wire disagree with nobody noticing.
end note

note bottom of BUG
  **403 is not xAI's word.** Measured: 401 for no
  or bad credentials, 400 for an incorrect key.
  A 403 here is the proxy's verdict, so the
  policy log names the rule — and it was
  captured, and never read.
end note

note right of LADDER
  **An empty prompt is today's ladder.** Reach a
  prompt, hold, assert nothing. Any string is
  typed in and the render scanned, because this
  session reached a prompt, held, and broke on
  first use — a clean PASS.
end note

legend bottom
  **What this file settles**
  ==
  A ""kind: sandbox"" Kit grants REACH from ""in.Detected"" and declares CREDENTIALS only
  for a service ""sbx secret ls"" already holds under its own name. proveo stores env-var
  names and refuses service names by design, so on any host nobody hand-primed the Kit
  allows ""x.ai"" and injects nothing — while the posture prints 'injected at the
  egress layer'.
  --
  The key still reached the wire, from the workspace "".env"" the prelude sources with
  ""set -a"". Two credential paths, no shared view. **403 is not the provider's answer to
  a bad key** (401/401/400, measured), so it is a proxy verdict and the captured
  ""policy-log.json"" names the rule.
  ==
  **The ladder could not have caught it**: every rung asserts 'reached a prompt and held',
  and this session did both. ""PROVEO_LADDER_PROMPT"" makes a rung spend the credential.
  --
  **Still open**: which rule produced the 403; whether a bare host needs a "":443"" suffix
  (docker/sbx-releases#319, #140, #189); whether ""*.x.ai"" is accepted in ""inject[].domain"".
end legend
@enduml
